1. SIBLING PARITY -- N/A: this repair changes the detector only.  The fix and its arms are the ones tables 1-4 measured.

2. CLAIM -> ROW.  The v5 header's enumeration names, for each effect and each listed value, the session(s) holding it.
   Every listed cell has ONE one-axis edit in this table, GENERATED from the listing rather than chosen
   (mutants549_t5.py, CELLS: keeps / first announce / silence / name / read / accept, over width, previous selector,
   COMMAND and latch, plus the effect-4 cells V and K hold).  CELLMAP.out maps each generated cell to its mutant; 13
   coincide in text with a table 2-4 edit and are not built twice.
   *** FOUND WHILE BUILDING THIS TABLE -- A WRONG RECORD OF MINE (L4).  Table 4 built NO one-axis announce edit for
   previous selectors 2, 3, 4, 6 or 7, nor for the single widths sb, sh or sd, while the v4 header said "the kill of each
   cell's one-axis edit is measured in regress/artifacts/fbctrlportkill_20260924/table4/TABLE.out".  The X sessions HELD
   those cells; no edit MEASURED them.  Generating the edits from the listing is the repair: a cell with no generated
   edit cannot be listed. ***
   Also a records fix the Fable adjudication named: closing2/f2_brief.md section 5a lists T_D9c_serial1 among the carried
   reds AND among the fourteen at the total; table 4 itself reconciles (14 at 94/94, 101 = 87 + 14) -- the stray is in
