3. GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD -- the floor, as Fable ruling 1 states it.  The PORT arm's body tests the access direction,
   `idata >= DEV_FBCTRL_NPORTS` (all 64 bits) and `!d->warned_port`, and reads and writes `current_port`.  Every cell of
   those is held: the value's class, width and magnitude; the latch unset and set; a read and a write.  The previous
   selector's VALUE, COMMAND and the data cells are not tested by the body: off-floor, held only as listed.
   No disagreeing-state row is owed: warned_port is written at one site (the refusal block) and read at one (its test).

4. CHANNEL, per NEW row -- the mutant(s) it exists to kill, and the observable that differs under them:
   X2 X6 X7 name rows       CELL_name_w2 / w1, CELL_name_p2 / p6 / p7, CF2_G_mask8 (X7: 0x100 -> 0x0): the first
                            announce's value text
